ction polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Matt Van Epps (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Tennessee's 7th District is a rematch of sorts between incumbent Republican Matt Van Epps and Democrat Darden Copeland, a Nashville businessman. The district leans Republican by about eleven points, and Van Epps enters with the advantages of incumbency, a large fundraising lead, and heavy outside support on his side. Copeland has raised a respectable sum for a challenger and has pressed an ethics complaint alleging improper use of taxpayer resources for campaign purposes, but independent spending has also flowed against him.\n\nEvery major race rater calls this Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Van Epps roughly a 96 percent chance of winning. Democrats' hopes rest on a strong midterm environment and the ethics controversy, but no public polling suggests the race is close. The forecast expects Van Epps to win by a comfortable double-digit margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0399, "margin": -11.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0635, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0506, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0318, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0486, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0413, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.049, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0174, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0197, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0585, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0233, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0193, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0334, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0457, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0518, "margin": -11.0}